# Gonti, Night Minister (cast on turn 1 with Black Lotus and a Mox Jet) attacks on turn 3 and deals 3 combat damage to Bot2: its
# controller looks at the top card of Bot2's library and exiles it face down (Bot2's library goes 12 -> 11). Bot1 casts that
# Lightning Bolt from exile with its Mox Jet's black mana in place of {R} (any type of mana can be spent) - a spell Bot1 does not own -
# so Bot1, the player who cast it, creates a Treasure token (CR 111.10a): Bot2 gets none, and Bot2 takes 3 from its own card. Casting its own Mox Jet and Gonti earlier made no Treasure.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Jet
Gonti, Night Minister
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x8
Lightning Bolt
Island x11

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Black)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Gonti, Night Minister.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Treasure Token = (absent)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Gonti, Night Minister > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot2.Life = 17
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Exile.Count = 1
? Bot2.Library.Count = 11
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Exile.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield = Gonti, Night Minister; Mox Jet; Treasure Token
Bot2.Battlefield.Treasure Token = (absent)
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 14
